DATA TRAINING HUB (DTH)
MISSION STATEMENT AND ARCHITECTURE ALIGNMENT DOCUMENT
Purpose
The Data Training Hub (DTH) exists to evolve from a mixed, single‑layer codebase into a clean, two‑layer, multi‑agent system built on the Three‑Zone Agent Pattern: Constitution, Runtime Pipeline, and Learning Loop. The mission is to create a stable backend runtime, a modular renderer ecosystem, and a closed‑loop agent architecture capable of classification, reasoning, evaluation, human‑simulated approval, and continuous rule learning.
Strategic Objective
Transform DTH into a fully aligned implementation of the Agent Pattern:
1. Constitution Layer: A unified source of truth containing rules, policies, constraints, diagnostics, and system integrity checks.
2. Runtime Pipeline: A structured inference flow consisting of Acting Agents, a Critic Agent, an ALF human‑simulator layer, and a central orchestrator.
3. Learning Loop: A feedback system that captures exceptions, updates rules, and evolves the Constitution over time.
